{"case_id":"T8099","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API entry point","error-state propagation","input semantics"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["simdjson_result<dom::array>::at_path","simdjson_result<dom::element>::at_path","simdjson_result<dom::object>::at_path"],"reason":"H0 exercises dom::element::at_pointer only after parser.parse and res.get succeed. It never calls any changed at_path overload and deliberately returns when res.error() is set, so it cannot test the newly guarded behavior where an already-errored simdjson_result must return error() before json_path_to_pointer_conversion processes attacker-controlled path input.","evidence":["H0 calls root.at_pointer(strings[1]); it contains no at_path call.","H0 returns immediately on res.error() and on res.get(root), preventing an errored simdjson_result<dom::element> from reaching at_path.","Each changed function adds `if (error()) { return error(); }` before `json_path_to_pointer_conversion(json_path)`.","The changed API exists separately for simdjson_result<dom::array>, simdjson_result<dom::element>, and simdjson_result<dom::object>, while H0 exercises none of those at_path wrappers."],"recommended_action":"Add fuzz coverage that supplies arbitrary JSON paths to all three simdjson_result<dom::array>::at_path, simdjson_result<dom::element>::at_path, and simdjson_result<dom::object>::at_path overloads, including calls on results already carrying errors, and verify that the original error is propagated without path conversion."}
